Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 00:28:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] U08 review: axe waits for the app, the hero gate is
 guarded, the portrait script fails cleanly

- ci.yml: the Axe step passes --load-delay 1000. On "/" React now mounts
  once the static hero's paint is recorded (up to 300 ms after the bundle
  runs), so "load" can come first when the portrait answers quickly; axe
  then audits the static shell, which has no <main>, and fails
  landmark-one-main and region. Reproduced in 1 of 15 emulated runs at
  delay 0, none at 1000. The step has been skipped while Lighthouse
  failed; with U08 it runs again.
- static-hero.test.ts: a guard that the marker sits inside #lw-shell, the
  prerendered hero is a section.home-hero (the gate's selector), and the
  portrait is fetchpriority low in both Home.tsx and prerender-heads.mjs.
- bring-portrait-home.mjs: an unreachable URL and a second run after the
  move now end with a plain message instead of a stack trace or an ENOENT
  on the site path.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JuCQ8kZ25i9zRwNgk6bh4e
